00:02:27.867 --> 00:02:31.680
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:32.517 --> 00:02:35.831
Visal, this is our last unit. What are your plans?

48
00:02:36.917 --> 00:02:41.148
I'm going to study abroad. I will help my community when I return.

49
00:02:42.250 --> 00:02:43.866
What are you doing next month?

50
00:02:44.950 --> 00:02:47.646
I'm taking my IELTS exam on the fifteenth.

51
00:02:48.750 --> 00:02:49.844
Are you ready?

52
00:02:50.950 --> 00:02:57.074
Yes! I've learned many skills, and I will use them to contribute to the world.

53
00:02:58.233 --> 00:02:59.757
Part three: grammar.

54
00:03:00.617 --> 00:03:03.243
Grammar focus: Future forms review.

55
00:03:03.543 --> 00:03:04.707
Look at the pattern.

56
00:03:05.417 --> 00:03:06.917
I'm going to study abroad.

57
00:03:07.817 --> 00:03:09.468
I will help my community.

58
00:03:10.383 --> 00:03:12.267
I'm taking my exam next month.

59
00:03:13.233 --> 00:03:19.006
Use 'going to' for plans, 'will' for promises and predictions, and the present continuous for fixed arrangements.

60
00:03:19.750 --> 00:03:23.203
Be careful! Don't say: I going to study abroad.

61
00:03:25.167 --> 00:03:27.259
Say: I'm going to study abroad.

62
00:03:27.559 --> 00:03:29.303
Don't forget 'am' before 'going to'.

63
00:03:30.100 --> 00:03:32.601
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:33.400 --> 00:03:34.587
Ready for the World.

65
00:03:34.887 --> 00:03:37.955
This year, we explored big ideas about our world.

66
00:03:38.967 --> 00:03:41.570
We learned skills, values and confidence.

67
00:03:42.567 --> 00:03:44.520
I'm going to keep learning every day.

68
00:03:45.533 --> 00:03:47.986
I will take responsibility for my future.

69
00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:52.172
As global citizens, we are ready to contribute.

70
00:03:53.267 --> 00:03:57.083
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:57.917 --> 00:03:59.789
I'm blank to study abroad.

72
00:04:00.089 --> 00:04:03.034
A, going. B, will. C, go.

73
00:04:06.600 --> 00:04:08.750
The answer is A: going.

74
00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:13.240
A person who cares about the whole world is a global blank.

75
00:04:13.540 --> 00:04:16.903
A, citizen. B, skill. C, value.

76
00:04:20.467 --> 00:04:22.431
The answer is A: citizen.

77
00:04:23.583 --> 00:04:25.734
To give help or ideas is to blank.

78
00:04:26.034 --> 00:04:29.757
A, contribute. B, ready. C, confide.

79
00:04:33.300 --> 00:04:35.346
The answer is A: contribute.

80
00:04:36.533 --> 00:04:39.720
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:40.583 --> 00:04:42.583
How will you contribute to the world?

82
00:04:51.383 --> 00:04:52.791
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:53.091 --> 00:05:00.712
I'm going to become a doctor. I will work in rural areas, and I will help people who cannot reach a hospital easily.

84
00:05:01.012 --> 00:05:02.617
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:05:03.517 --> 00:05:07.736
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and future forms review.

86
00:05:08.036 --> 00:05:14.023
Today's value is global citizenship. We all share one world. Help people near and far.

87
00:05:14.323 --> 00:05:19.881
Congratulations! You have finished Online B two, Book three. See you in Online C one!

88
00:05:20.181 --> 00:05:22.775
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

